{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-257299-r4630284","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Murghi Korma (Chicken Korma)","sourcePageId":257299,"sourceRevision":"4630284","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-04-12T20:27:21Z","sourceRevisionUser":"AdoniTzedek","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Murghi%20Korma%20(Chicken%20Korma)&oldid=4630284","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:09:24.376Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Bengali recipes","Category:Halal recipes","Category:Indian recipes","Category:Kosher for Passover recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using almond","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using cardamom","Category:Recipes using cinnamon stick","Category:Recipes using clove","Category:Recipes using coconut cream","Category:Recipes using coriander","Category:Recipes using ginger paste","Category:Recipes using ground cumin","Category:Recipes using sugar","Category:Recipes using whole chicken"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"47c303e7fdf7fb331069ec5a80ca38ba29cc5a1305fa58e9ce3eeec26e1c8db4","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{recipesummary\n| category = Indian recipes\n| servings = 4\n| time = 50 minutes\n| difficulty = 3\n}}\n{{Recipe}}|[[Cookbook:Asian Cuisine|South Asian cuisines]]\n==Ingredients==\n\n=== Marinade ===\n* Whole chicken, skinned and cut into medium pieces; ideally into 6 pieces if using baby chicken\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]] paste\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]] paste\n* 1½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Coriander|coriander]] powder\n* 1½ tsp [[Cookbook:Cumin|cumin]] powder\n* ½ tsp [[Cookbook:Nutmeg|nutmeg]] powder (optional)\n* 1 tbsp Greek [[Cookbook:Yogurt|yogurt]]\n\n=== Cooking ===\n* 2 medium sized [[Cookbook:Onion|onions]], chopped\n* 6–8 [[Cookbook:Cardamom|cardamom]] pods\n* 3–5 whole [[Cookbook:Clove|cloves]]\n* 1 medium [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]] stick\n* [[Cookbook:Pepper|Black pepper]], crushed, according to taste\n* 1–2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Ghee|ghee]] or [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]], according to taste\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n\n=== Serving ===\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Coconut Cream|coconut cream]]/crushed coconut\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] single [[Cookbook:Cream|cream]]\n* 4–6 threads [[Cookbook:Saffron|saffron]]\n* A few drops [[Cookbook:Rosewater|rosewater]] (optional)\n* 1 tbsp toasted flakes of [[Cookbook:Almond|almonds]] for decoration (optional)\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Combine the chicken with all the marinade ingredients, cover the bowl with [[Cookbook:Plastic Wrap|cling film]], and leave in the fridge to [[Cookbook:Marinating|marinate]] for 1–3 hours.\n#[[Cookbook:Frying|Fry]] the onions in ghee until it starts to turn brown but still soft. Do not fry to crispiness. Take out the onion with slotted spoon and set aside.\n#Add the marinated chicken to the hot ghee and cook over medium heat.\n#Dry toast the whole spices in a hot [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|frying pan]] for 1 minute until aromatic.\n#Add the whole spices and black pepper to the chicken.\n#Stir occasionally and cook covered.\n#When water starts to separate from the chicken, add coconut cream, salt and sugar.\n#Add boiling water if chicken starts to dry up before its cooked.\n#Warm the single cream in microwave and add saffron to it.\n#Stir in cream when almost cooked.\n#Remove from the heat, and serve with fried onions, rose water, and almonds.\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n* Serve with warm pilaf rice.\n* Korma, being a mild dish, can be a good introduction to South Asian cuisines, especially for those who like to avoid too spicy or too hot dishes.\n* Ethnic ingredient shops often sell premade fried onion packs.\n[[Category:Indian recipes|Murghi Korma]]\n[[Category:Recipes using whole chicken]]\n[[Category:Bengali recipes|Murghi Korma]]\n[[Category:Recipes using almond]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cardamom]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cinnamon stick]]\n[[Category:Recipes using clove]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coconut cream]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coriander]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ginger paste]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cumin]]\n[[Category:Halal recipes]]\n[[Category:Kosher for Passover recipes]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Murghi Korma (Chicken Korma)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"4","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"Whole chicken, skinned and cut into medium pieces; ideally into 6 pieces if using baby chicken","sourceText":"Whole chicken, skinned and cut into medium pieces; ideally into 6 pieces if using baby chicken","amountText":"Whole chicken, skinned and cut into medium pieces; ideally into 6 pieces if using baby chicken","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 tbsp ginger paste","sourceText":"1 tbsp ginger paste","amountText":"1 tbsp ginger paste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 tbsp garlic paste","sourceText":"1 tbsp garlic paste","amountText":"1 tbsp garlic paste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1½ tsp coriander powder","sourceText":"1½ tsp coriander powder",